DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20250415
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20250416
SUMMARY:Michigan: Form 807 (composite) due
DESCRIPTION:Michigan does not require a separate entity-level informational
  return akin to 1065/1120-S for most PTEs - the composite Form 807 return i
 s the relevant filing\, due April 15 (same as the individual MI-1040 due da
 te). MI's Flow-Through Entity (FTE) elective tax has its own separate retur
 n (Form 5772/5773). | Michigan does not require a separate entity-level inf
 ormational return akin to 1065/1120-S for most PTEs - the composite Form 80
 7 return is the relevant filing\, due April 15 (same as the individual MI-1
 040 due date). MI's Flow-Through Entity (FTE) elective tax has its own sepa
 rate return (Form 5772/5773). Follows the MI-1040 individual extension proc
 ess (Form 4). | Authority: Michigan Department of Treasury\, direct fetch t
 his session: "The composite filing due date corresponds with the due date o
 f the Michigan Individual Income Tax Return (MI-1040)\, generally due on Ap
 ril 15th after the close of the calendar year." | Source: https://www.michi
 gan.gov/taxes/0\,4676\,7-238-75545_43715-400944--\,00.html | This date is c
 omputed from a recurrence rule and may not reflect a later-announced change
 \; confirm against the cited source before relying on it.
