SUMMARY:Hawaii: N-20 (partnership) / N-35 (S-corp) due
DESCRIPTION:Hawaii partnership return due the 20th day of the 4th month aft
 er year-end - a real outlier (20th of the month\, not the 15th) from the pa
 ttern most other states use. | Hawaii partnership return due the 20th day o
 f the 4th month after year-end - a real outlier (20th of the month\, not th
 e 15th) from the pattern most other states use. Automatic 6-month extension
  without filing an application\, per Hawaii Administrative Rules 18-235-98\
 ; payment of tax due is still required by the original date. | Authority: H
 awaii Department of Taxation\, direct fetch this session: "Returns must be 
 filed on or before the 20th day of the fourth month following the close of 
 the taxable year" and "Section 18-235-98\, Hawaii Administrative Rules\, al
 lows an automatic six-month extension of time to file a return without fili
 ng an application for extension." | Source: https://files.hawaii.gov/tax/fo
 rms/current/n20ins.pdf | This date is computed from a recurrence rule and m
