SUMMARY:Iowa: State sales & use tax return due
DESCRIPTION:Iowa's sales/use tax filing frequency is NOT quarterly - confir
 med directly against the Iowa Administrative Code (701-202.1(423)\, publish
 ed by the Iowa Legislature at legis.iowa.gov\, the state's own official cod
 ification): "A retailer owing $1\,200 or more in sales or use tax per calen
 dar year shall file a sales and use tax return once per month. This monthly
  return is due on or before the last day of the month following the end of 
 the month in which the tax was collected. A retailer owing less than $1\,20
 0 in sales or use tax per calendar year shall file a sales and use tax retu
 rn at least once per annual year\, due on or before January 31 for the prio
 r calendar year." The four dates below are representative monthly due dates
  (last day of the following month) spread across 2026 for the standard $1\,
 200-or-more monthly filer\, not literal calendar quarters - Iowa has no qua
 rterly sales tax filing option under current rule. Small filers under the $
 1\,200 annual threshold instead file once a year\, by January 31. | Monthly
  return for April 2026 sales\, due the last day of May 2026 (illustrative m
 onthly occurrence). Iowa's sales/use tax filing frequency is NOT quarterly 
 - confirmed directly against the Iowa Administrative Code (701-202.1(423)\,
  published by the Iowa Legislature at legis.iowa.gov\, the state's own offi
 cial codification): "A retailer owing $1\,200 or more in sales or use tax p
 er calendar year shall file a sales and use tax return once per month. This
  monthly return is due on or before the last day of the month following the
  end of the month in which the tax was collected. A retailer owing less tha
 n $1\,200 in sales or use tax per calendar year shall file a sales and use 
 tax return at least once per annual year\, due on or before January 31 for 
 the prior calendar year." The four dates below are representative monthly d
 ue dates (last day of the following month) spread across 2026 for the stand
 ard $1\,200-or-more monthly filer\, not literal calendar quarters - Iowa ha
 s no quarterly sales tax filing option under current rule. Small filers und
 er the $1\,200 annual threshold instead file once a year\, by January 31. |
  Authority: Iowa Administrative Code 701-202.1(423)\, official codification
  published by the Iowa Legislature (legis.iowa.gov) | Source: https://www.l
 egis.iowa.gov/docs/iac/chapter/701.202.pdf | This date is computed from a r
 ecurrence rule and may not reflect a later-announced change\; confirm again
 st the cited source before relying on it.
